    "readout_text": "To determine how many miles from City A Alicia and Beth will meet, we analyze their combined motion and use the relationship between distance, speed, and time.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Motion\n\n- **Distance between cities A and B:** 45 miles  \n- **Alicia's speed:** 18 mph (from A to B)  \n- **Beth's speed:** 12 mph (from B to A)  \n- **Both start at the same time and move toward each other.**\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Relative Speed\n\nWhen two objects move toward each other, their **relative speed** is the **sum** of their individual speeds:\n\n$$\n\\text{Relative speed} = 18\\, \\text{mph} + 12\\, \\text{mph} = 30\\, \\text{mph}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Time Until Meeting\n\nThe time it takes for them to meet is the total distance divided by their relative speed:\n\n$$\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{45\\, \\text{miles}}{30\\, \\text{mph}} = 1.5\\, \\text{hours}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Distance from City A\n\nAlicia is moving toward City B at 18 mph, so the distance she covers in 1.5 hours is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Distance from A} = 18\\, \\text{mph} \\times 1.5\\, \\text{hours} = 27\\, \\text{miles}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Verification\n\nTo ensure correctness, we check how far Beth would travel in the same time:\n\n$$\n\\text{Distance from B} = 12\\, \\text{mph} \\times 1.5\\, \\text{hours} = 18\\, \\text{miles}\n$$\n\nAdding these distances:\n\n$$\n27\\, \\text{miles} + 18\\, \\text{miles} = 45\\, \\text{miles}\n$$\n\nThis confirms that the total distance between A and B is accounted for, and the meeting point is indeed 27 miles from City A.\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\n$$\n\\boxed{27}\n$$\n\n\\confidence{Almost certain}",
